---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy policy | SecretariatPro"
  description="Information about how SecretariatPro processes personal data."
>
  <section class="page-hero legal-hero">
    <div class="shell" data-reveal>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>

      <p class="lead">
        Information about how we process and protect your personal data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section legal-section">
    <div class="shell legal-shell">
      <article class="legal-content" data-reveal>

        <section>
          <h2>Data controller</h2>

          <p>
            The controller responsible for personal data relating to this
            website is:
          </p>

          <dl class="legal-data">
            <div>
              <dt>Controller</dt>
              <dd>Alejandro García Reñones</dd>
            </div>

            <div>
              <dt>Trading name</dt>
              <dd>SecretariatPro</dd>
            </div>

            <div>
              <dt>Address</dt>
              <dd>Calle Sierra de Atapuerca 31, Madrid, Spain</dd>
            </div>

            <div>
              <dt>Email</dt>
              <dd>
                <a href="mailto:a.garciarenones@gmail.com">
                  a.garciarenones@gmail.com
                </a>
              </dd>
            </div>

            <div>
              <dt>Website</dt>
              <dd>secretariatproapp.com</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data we process</h2>

          <p>
            At present, the SecretariatPro website does not provide public
            registration, contracting or demo-request forms.
          </p>

          <p>
            We may process information that you voluntarily provide when
            contacting us by email, including, for example, your name,
            email address, organisation, role and the content of your
            communication.
          </p>

          <p>
            Technology providers used to operate and secure the website
            may also process certain technical information, such as IP
            address, date and time of access, browser information or
            technical logs required to provide the service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How we use your data</h2>

          <p>
            Personal data provided may be processed to respond to enquiries
            and requests, maintain communications relating to SecretariatPro,
            deal with technical or commercial matters requested by the
            individual and ensure the security and correct operation of
            the website.
          </p>

          <p>
            We will not use personal data for purposes incompatible with
            those for which it was obtained.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Legal basis</h2>

          <p>
            When you voluntarily contact SecretariatPro, the processing
            required to respond to your communication is based on dealing
            with the request you have made.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where the communication relates to a potential contract or
            provision of services, processing may be necessary to take
            pre-contractual steps requested by you.
          </p>

          <p>
            Certain technical processing activities related to the
            security, maintenance and correct operation of the website may
            be based on the controller's legitimate interest in ensuring
            the integrity and availability of the service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data retention</h2>

          <p>
            Data will be retained for as long as necessary to fulfil the
            purpose for which it was provided.
          </p>

          <p>
            It may subsequently be retained in a restricted form for the
            periods required to address potential legal liabilities.
          </p>

          <p>
            When the data is no longer necessary and there is no legal
            obligation requiring its retention, it will be deleted.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Recipients and service providers</h2>

          <p>
            SecretariatPro does not sell personal data or disclose it to
            third parties for advertising purposes.
          </p>

          <p>
            Certain technology providers may access or process information
            where necessary to provide hosting, infrastructure, email,
            security or other technical services required for
            SecretariatPro to operate.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where those providers act as data processors, the safeguards
            required by applicable data protection legislation will be
            adopted.
          </p>

          <p>
            Data may also be disclosed where required by law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>International transfers</h2>

          <p>
            Some technology providers used by SecretariatPro may provide
            their services from countries outside the European Economic
            Area.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where an international transfer of personal data takes place,
            the safeguards required by applicable data protection
            legislation will be applied.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your rights</h2>

          <p>
            Where applicable, you may exercise your rights of access,
            rectification, erasure, objection, restriction of processing
            and data portability.
          </p>

          <p>
            To exercise these rights, you may send a request to:
          </p>

          <p>
            <a href="mailto:a.garciarenones@gmail.com">
              a.garciarenones@gmail.com
            </a>
          </p>

          <p>
            The request must allow the individual to be properly identified
            and specify the right they wish to exercise.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Complaints</h2>

          <p>
            If you believe that the processing of your personal data does
            not comply with applicable legislation, you may lodge a
            complaint with the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD).
          </p>

          <p>
            Further information is available at
            <a
              href="https://www.aepd.es"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              www.aepd.es
            </a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Security</h2>

          <p>
            SecretariatPro applies reasonable technical and organisational
            measures designed to protect personal data against unauthorised
            access, loss, alteration or improper disclosure.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

          <p>
            This Privacy Policy may be updated when the services provided,
            the processing activities or applicable legislation change.
          </p>

          <p>
            The version published on this page will be the version in force
            at any given time.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-update">
          <p>Last updated: September 2026.</p>
        </section>

      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
